<CaseStudyLayout
  title="nuVector"
  description="A redesign and rebuild of nuVector's corporate website on Astro: services, client proof, case studies and a blog, all pointed at one action, requesting a demo."
  client="nuVector LLC (Atlanta, Georgia)"
  role="Design & front-end development"
  year="2024 to 2025"
  slides={[
    {
      title: 'Hero, services and clients',
      src: '/videos/web-development-project-nuvector-intro.mp4',
      poster: '/images/nuvector-intro.webp',
    },
    {
      title: 'Platform, case studies and about',
      src: '/videos/web-development-project-nuvector-platform.mp4',
      poster: '/images/nuvector-platform.webp',
    },
    {
      title: 'Blog and demo request',
      src: '/videos/web-development-project-nuvector-blog.mp4',
      poster: '/images/nuvector-blog.webp',
    },
  ]}
  highlights={[
    { value: 'Rebuilt on Astro', label: 'Static pages, fast loads, nothing to patch' },
    { value: 'Proof up front', label: 'Volvo, ZF, Sonoco and other client logos above the fold' },
    { value: '1 CTA', label: 'Request a demo, repeated where decisions happen' },
  ]}
  overview={[
    'nuVector builds returnable asset management software for manufacturers and logistics teams: the containers, racks and tooling that leave a plant and are supposed to come back. I worked there as a front-end developer and later on SEO and marketing, so I knew the audience. The corporate site had a different job from the <a class="text-link" href="/web-developer-project-loopmanager">LoopManager product site</a>: <strong>make nuVector look like a company you would trust with your supply chain, then get the visitor to book a demo.</strong> I redesigned and rebuilt it around that.',
    'The page opens with a clear promise ("next-level asset management", "your supply chain partner in Atlanta") and a demo button, then earns it: a services block covering supply chain optimization, workflow tracking and data infrastructure, a strip of client logos including Volvo, Warner Bros. Discovery, Sonoco, Regal and ZF, a platform feature grid, a case studies section, a short company story, and a blog. A full-width "Request a free demo" section and a contact-rich footer close it out. The orange-and-charcoal brand and the geometric "n" mark carry through every section.',
    'It is built on Astro as a static site, so pages load fast and there is no plugin stack to maintain. The blog is where the SEO work lives: posts on RFID readers, construction asset tracking and returnable asset trends, each structured to rank for a specific search and to end at the demo form.',
    'Together with the LoopManager product site, this gave nuVector one consistent, fast web presence from company story to product to demo request.',
  ]}
  tools={['Astro', 'HTML & CSS', 'JavaScript', 'TypeScript', 'Figma', 'SEO']}
/>
